  "sources": {
    "nfp_cpi_ppi": "BLS Schedule of Selected Releases, https://www.bls.gov/schedule/YEAR/, copies retrieved via web.archive.org on 2026-10-10 because bls.gov returned HTTP 403. Kept only 8:30 AM ET rows named Employment Situation for, Consumer Price Index for, or Producer Price Index for.",
    "fomc": "Federal Reserve statement links monetaryYYYYMMDDa.htm on https://www.federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/fomccalendars.htm plus fomchistorical2019.htm and fomchistorical2020.htm, retrieved 2026-10-10. Headings that say notation vote are fomc_notation, not decision days.",
    "vix": "Cboe VIX History CSV https://cdn.cboe.com/api/global/us_indices/daily_prices/VIX_History.csv retrieved 2026-10-10. Closes through 2026-10-09.",
    "gaps": [
      "The archived 2025 BLS schedule has no Consumer Price Index row for the October 2025 reference month and no Employment Situation or Producer Price Index row for the October 2025 reference month. September 2025 CPI was released 2025-10-24, September 2025 employment on 2025-11-20, and September 2025 PPI on 2025-11-25. Those delayed dates are tagged. The missing October reference month is the funding-lapse gap, not a parser miss.",
      "ISM dates use the standing first-and-third business-day rule at 10:00 AM ET. A published ISM shift off that rule is not listed.",
      "Half days use the NYSE 1:00 PM ET early-close pattern. The archived hours page (web.archive.org, 2026) states early closes for November 27, 2026, December 24, 2026, and July 3, 2028. A historical early close outside that pattern is not listed. CME Globex halt times are not bar-verified.",
      "FOMC unscheduled statements that are not notation votes, including 2019-10-11, 2020-03-03, and 2020-03-15, are decision days. 2020-03-15 was a Sunday and is applied to the Monday cash session."
    ]
  },
